GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `What is the most I can receive for one application` IS
    `the s 24 maximum total for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`)

§§ `Part 3, division 3.3 -- what each payment can be`

@export What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need: cleaning a homicide scene, security, relocation, emergency medical costs (s 26, Regulation s 6)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `what cleaning the homicide scene costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What cleaning the scene of the homicide has cost or will cost you, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `what my personal security measures cost` IS A NUMBER @desc What measures for your personal security (such as locks, alarms or cameras) have cost or will cost, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `what moving for my security costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What relocating for your personal security has cost or will cost, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my emergency medical costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Emergency medical costs and related services that would help your recovery, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `I cannot afford the emergency treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do not have the financial ability to pay for that emergency treatment or service yourself
      `immediate need payments already made for this act` IS A NUMBER @desc Immediate need payments already made to anyone, you or others, for the same act of violence, in Australian dollars (0 if none or not known)
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be paid for an immediate need` IS
    `the immediate need payment answer for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`)
        (`Immediate need claim` WITH
            `cleaning the scene of a homicide`                 IS `what cleaning the homicide scene costs`
            `measures for the personal security of a victim`   IS `what my personal security measures cost`
            `relocation for the personal security of a victim` IS `what moving for my security costs`
            `emergency medical costs and related services`     IS `my emergency medical costs`
            `the applicant does not have the financial ability to pay for the treatment or service` IS `I cannot afford the emergency treatment`
            `immediate need payments already made to anyone for the same act of violence` IS `immediate need payments already made for this act`)

@export What is the most I can be paid for this kind of economic loss, such as lost earnings, medical costs or counselling (s 27, Regulation s 7)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `the kind of loss` IS AN `Economic loss kind` @desc The kind of economic loss. One of: "expenses for counselling or other psychological support"; "expenses, other than legal costs, of making the application"; "medical and dental expenses"; "travel expenses"; "justice related expenses"; "loss of actual earnings"; "reasonable expenses of the parent or carer of a primary victim"; "other expenses in exceptional circumstances"; "loss of or damage to personal items"
      `the amount of that loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of that loss, in Australian dollars
      `I could not get counselling through the victims services scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not able to get appropriate counselling or other psychological support under the victims services scheme (Victims of Crime Act 1994, s 19)
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be paid for this economic loss` IS
    `the economic loss payment answer for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`) `the kind of loss` `the amount of that loss` `I could not get counselling through the victims services scheme`

@export What recognition payment can I get for this offence (ss 28 to 30, Regulation ss 8 to 10)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `the offence for a recognition payment` IS A `Table 8 offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act of violence happened, as table 8 of the Regulation describes it. One of: "a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit homicide"; "a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years"; "an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more"; "a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years"; "an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm"; "robbery in company or with an offensive weapon"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years"; "an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm"; "an offence involving deprivation of liberty, including kidnapping and forcible confinement"; "an offence against the person not resulting in actual bodily harm"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years"; "an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm"; "none of the offences in table 8"
      `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether section 66 (1) (b) of the Crimes Act 1900 applies to the offence (it matters only for a sexual offence punishable by 10 to 14 years; if unsure, answer no)
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `What recognition payment can I get` IS
    `the recognition payment answer for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`) `the offence for a recognition payment` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies to the offence`

-- All the claims of one application together, within the s 24 maximum, less the s 47 reductions, and nothing if s 45 applies.

@export Taking all my claims together, what is the most financial assistance I can be given on my application (ss 24, 26 to 30, 45 and 47)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `what cleaning the homicide scene costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What cleaning the scene of the homicide has cost or will cost you, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `what my personal security measures cost` IS A NUMBER @desc What measures for your personal security (such as locks, alarms or cameras) have cost or will cost, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `what moving for my security costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What relocating for your personal security has cost or will cost, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my emergency medical costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Emergency medical costs and related services that would help your recovery, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `I cannot afford the emergency treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do not have the financial ability to pay for that emergency treatment or service yourself
      `immediate need payments already made for this act` IS A NUMBER @desc Immediate need payments already made to anyone, you or others, for the same act of violence, in Australian dollars (0 if none or not known)
      `my counselling costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Expenses for counselling or other psychological support, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my costs of applying, not legal costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Expenses of making this application, other than legal costs, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my medical and dental expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Medical and dental expenses, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my travel expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Travel expenses, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my justice related expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Justice related expenses, such as costs of attending court, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my lost earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Actual earnings lost, including earnings lost by the parent or carer of the person injured, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my parent's or carer's reasonable expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Reasonable expenses of the parent or carer of the person injured, caused by the act of violence, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `my other expenses in exceptional circumstances` IS A NUMBER @desc Other expenses in exceptional circumstances, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `what my lost or damaged personal items are worth` IS A NUMBER @desc The loss of, or damage to, your personal items, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `I could not get counselling through the victims services scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not able to get appropriate counselling or other psychological support under the victims services scheme (Victims of Crime Act 1994, s 19)
      `I claim a recognition payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims a recognition payment
      `the offence for a recognition payment` IS A `Table 8 offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act of violence happened, as table 8 of the Regulation describes it. One of: "a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit homicide"; "a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years"; "an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 14 years or more"; "a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years"; "an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm"; "robbery in company or with an offensive weapon"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for 10 years or more, but less than 14 years"; "an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in grievous bodily harm"; "an offence involving deprivation of liberty, including kidnapping and forcible confinement"; "an offence against the person not resulting in actual bodily harm"; "an attempt or conspiracy to commit a sexual offence punishable by imprisonment for less than 10 years"; "an attempt, threat or conspiracy to commit an offence against the person resulting in actual bodily harm"; "none of the offences in table 8"
      `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether section 66 (1) (b) of the Crimes Act 1900 applies to the offence (it matters only for a sexual offence punishable by 10 to 14 years; if unsure, answer no)
      `the commissioner finds I conspired with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you conspired with the person responsible for the act of violence (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds my serious crime was the main reason for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you were involved in a serious crime when the act happened and that crime was the main reason for it (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds the act was related to a serious crime by the person injured or killed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim (the person injured or killed); it matters only for a related victim (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds I unreasonably failed to help the police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police about the act (answer no if not)
      `payments I have received for the same harm or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Other payments you have received because of the act that cover the same harm or loss, such as damages, workers compensation, insurance or a reparation order, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `repayments I still owe under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount you were earlier required to repay under part 5 or part 6 of the Act and have not repaid, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the reduction for my contributory conduct` IS A NUMBER @desc The reduction the commissioner decides is appropriate for conduct of yours that contributed to the injury, took part in or encouraged the act, or failed to take reasonable steps to limit the injury, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be given on my application, all claims together` IS
    `the total financial assistance answer for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`)
        (`Immediate need claim` WITH
            `cleaning the scene of a homicide`                 IS `what cleaning the homicide scene costs`
            `measures for the personal security of a victim`   IS `what my personal security measures cost`
            `relocation for the personal security of a victim` IS `what moving for my security costs`
            `emergency medical costs and related services`     IS `my emergency medical costs`
            `the applicant does not have the financial ability to pay for the treatment or service` IS `I cannot afford the emergency treatment`
            `immediate need payments already made to anyone for the same act of violence` IS `immediate need payments already made for this act`)
        (`Economic loss claim` WITH
            `counselling or other psychological support` IS `my counselling costs`
            `expenses of making the application, other than legal costs` IS `my costs of applying, not legal costs`
            `medical and dental` IS `my medical and dental expenses`
            `travel` IS `my travel expenses`
            `justice related` IS `my justice related expenses`
            `actual earnings lost` IS `my lost earnings`
            `the parent's or carer's reasonable expenses` IS `my parent's or carer's reasonable expenses`
            `other expenses in exceptional circumstances claimed` IS `my other expenses in exceptional circumstances`
            `personal items lost or damaged` IS `what my lost or damaged personal items are worth`
            `counselling was not available under the victims services scheme` IS `I could not get counselling through the victims services scheme`)
        `I claim a recognition payment` `the offence for a recognition payment` `the Crimes Act s 66 (1) (b) applies to the offence`
        (`Conduct findings` WITH
            `the applicant conspired with the person responsible for the act` IS `the commissioner finds I conspired with the offender`
            `the applicant was involved in a serious crime that was the main reason the act occurred` IS `the commissioner finds my serious crime was the main reason for the act`
            `the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim` IS `the commissioner finds the act was related to a serious crime by the person injured or killed`
            `the applicant unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police` IS `the commissioner finds I unreasonably failed to help the police`)
        (`Reductions` WITH
            `associated payments covering the same harm or loss` IS `payments I have received for the same harm or loss`
            `outstanding repayment amounts under part 5 or part 6` IS `repayments I still owe under the Act`
            `the reduction for contributory conduct that the commissioner decides` IS `the reduction for my contributory conduct`)

§§ `Part 3, division 3.4 -- applying: the evidence, and the time`

-- `the s 31 evidence needed for` reads only the claims and the age of the offender from the application record, so its
-- other fields are fixed placeholders here.

@export What evidence that the act was reported must my application include (s 31)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `the offender was in a position of power, trust or authority over me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person responsible for the act was in a position of power, trust or authority over the person injured (you, if you are applying about your own injury)
      `I have impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, such as 2009-05-20
      `I did not report to police because of threats or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not report the act to police because someone threatened or intimidated you
      `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who carried out the act was under the age of criminal responsibility for the offence (not criminally responsible because of their age under the Criminal Code, s 25)
      `I claim an immediate need payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims an immediate need payment
      `I claim an economic loss payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims an economic loss payment
      `I claim a recognition payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims a recognition payment
GIVETH AN `Evidence answer`
DECIDE `What evidence of reporting must my application include` IS
    `the s 31 evidence needed for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`)
        (`Special reporting facts` WITH
            `the person responsible was in a position of power, trust or authority over the primary victim` IS `the offender was in a position of power, trust or authority over me`
            `the applicant has impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity` IS `I have impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity`
            `the applicant's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the applicant did not report to police because of threats or intimidation` IS `I did not report to police because of threats or intimidation`)
        (`Application facts` WITH
            `is in writing` IS TRUE
            `includes a contact address` IS TRUE
            `indicates the payments claimed` IS TRUE
            `claims an immediate need payment` IS `I claim an immediate need payment`
            `claims an economic loss payment` IS `I claim an economic loss payment`
            `claims a recognition payment in the application` IS `I claim a recognition payment`
            `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility` IS `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility`
            `the act was reported to a police officer` IS FALSE
            `the act was reported to a government agency` IS FALSE
            `the act was reported to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker` IS FALSE
            `the act was reported to an appropriately qualified non-government agency` IS FALSE)

@export Does my application meet the requirements of s 31: in writing, with a contact address, the payments claimed and the evidence of reporting?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `the offender was in a position of power, trust or authority over me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person responsible for the act was in a position of power, trust or authority over the person injured (you, if you are applying about your own injury)
      `I have impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, such as 2009-05-20
      `I did not report to police because of threats or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not report the act to police because someone threatened or intimidated you
      `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who carried out the act was under the age of criminal responsibility for the offence (not criminally responsible because of their age under the Criminal Code, s 25)
      `I claim an immediate need payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims an immediate need payment
      `I claim an economic loss payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims an economic loss payment
      `I claim a recognition payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application claims a recognition payment
      `my application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application is in writing
      `my application gives a contact address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application includes a contact address for you
      `my application says which payments I claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application says which financial assistance payments you want to claim
      `the act was reported to a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have evidence that the act of violence was reported to a police officer
      `I reported the act to a government agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have evidence that you reported the act to a government agency
      `I reported the act to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have evidence that you reported the act to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker
      `I reported the act to a non-government agency listed in the commissioner's guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have evidence that you reported the act to a non-government agency that the commissioner's guidelines specify as appropriately qualified (the guidelines are not part of this encoding; answer from what the commissioner tells you)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application meet the requirements of s 31` IS
    `the application complies with s 31 (2)` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`)
        (`Special reporting facts` WITH
            `the person responsible was in a position of power, trust or authority over the primary victim` IS `the offender was in a position of power, trust or authority over me`
            `the applicant has impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity` IS `I have impaired physical, psychological or intellectual capacity`
            `the applicant's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the applicant did not report to police because of threats or intimidation` IS `I did not report to police because of threats or intimidation`)
        (`Application facts` WITH
            `is in writing` IS `my application is in writing`
            `includes a contact address` IS `my application gives a contact address`
            `indicates the payments claimed` IS `my application says which payments I claim`
            `claims an immediate need payment` IS `I claim an immediate need payment`
            `claims an economic loss payment` IS `I claim an economic loss payment`
            `claims a recognition payment in the application` IS `I claim a recognition payment`
            `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility` IS `the offender was under the age of criminal responsibility`
            `the act was reported to a police officer` IS `the act was reported to a police officer`
            `the act was reported to a government agency` IS `I reported the act to a government agency`
            `the act was reported to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker` IS `I reported the act to a doctor, psychologist, counsellor or social worker`
            `the act was reported to an appropriately qualified non-government agency` IS `I reported the act to a non-government agency listed in the commissioner's guidelines`)

@export What is the last day to apply for financial assistance: 3 years after the act, or after I turn 18 (s 32 (1))?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, such as 2009-05-20
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to apply for financial assistance` IS
    `the last day to apply for financial assistance (s 32 (1))` `the day of the act of violence` `my date of birth`

@export Is my application for financial assistance in time, and if not, can the time be extended (s 32)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, such as 2009-05-20
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the application, such as 2027-06-30
GIVETH A `Time answer`
DECIDE `Is my application in time` IS
    `the s 32 answer for` `the day of the act of violence` `my date of birth` `the day I apply`

§§ `Part 3, division 3.6 -- when assistance is refused or reduced`

-- Situation: the commissioner has raised a disqualifying circumstance, or a reduction, on the application.

@export Must financial assistance be refused to me because of a disqualifying circumstance (s 45)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `my application is about` IS A `Capacity` @desc What your application is about. One of: "an injury to the applicant" (your own injury); "the death of a person killed by the act" (you apply because of the death of a partner, relative or someone you depended on)
      `my harm` IS A `Harm` @desc The harm you suffered. One of: "a physical injury, mental illness or mental disorder, or a disease, or the aggravation or recurrence of one"; "only a harm listed in s 9 (1) (c): unplanned pregnancy, a sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, or reduced capacity for sexual activity"; "no injury"
      `my harm came directly from the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your harm was a direct result of the act of violence done to you (answer no if you were harmed only by seeing it done to someone else, or by being a witness afterwards)
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `my relationship to the person who died` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship to the person who died, when they died. One of: "the domestic partner"; "an intimate partner who was not a domestic partner"; "a parent, guardian or step-parent" (not a guardian only because of a statutory office); "a child or stepchild, or a child of whom the person who died was the guardian"; "a brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, half-brother or half-sister" (including someone regarded as one under the traditions and customs of the Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community of the person who died); "another relationship, or none"
      `I depended on the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the person died, you depended on them wholly or partly for economic support, or would have but for an incapacity the act caused them, or you are their child born after their death who would have
      `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were present when the person was killed, or are a witness in the criminal investigation or a court proceeding about the killing
      `I took part in the homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the people who carried out the killing
      `the commissioner finds I conspired with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you conspired with the person responsible for the act of violence (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds my serious crime was the main reason for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you were involved in a serious crime when the act happened and that crime was the main reason for it (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds the act was related to a serious crime by the person injured or killed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim (the person injured or killed); it matters only for a related victim (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds I unreasonably failed to help the police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police about the act (answer no if not)
GIVETH A `Refusal answer`
DECIDE `Must financial assistance be refused to me` IS
    `the s 45 answer for` (`my victim facts from my answers` `the day of the act of violence` `the offence` `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` `my application is about` `my harm` `my harm came directly from the act` `whether anyone died` `my relationship to the person who died` `I depended on the person who died` `I was present at the homicide or am a witness about it` `I took part in the homicide`)
        (`Conduct findings` WITH
            `the applicant conspired with the person responsible for the act` IS `the commissioner finds I conspired with the offender`
            `the applicant was involved in a serious crime that was the main reason the act occurred` IS `the commissioner finds my serious crime was the main reason for the act`
            `the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim` IS `the commissioner finds the act was related to a serious crime by the person injured or killed`
            `the applicant unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police` IS `the commissioner finds I unreasonably failed to help the police`)

@export By how much must the commissioner reduce my financial assistance (s 47)?
GIVEN `payments I have received for the same harm or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc Other payments you have received because of the act that cover the same harm or loss, such as damages, workers compensation, insurance or a reparation order, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `repayments I still owe under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc Any amount you were earlier required to repay under part 5 or part 6 of the Act and have not repaid, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the reduction for my contributory conduct` IS A NUMBER @desc The reduction the commissioner decides is appropriate for conduct of yours that contributed to the injury, took part in or encouraged the act, or failed to take reasonable steps to limit the injury, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much must my assistance be reduced` IS
    `the s 47 reduction` (`Reductions` WITH
            `associated payments covering the same harm or loss` IS `payments I have received for the same harm or loss`
            `outstanding repayment amounts under part 5 or part 6` IS `repayments I still owe under the Act`
            `the reduction for contributory conduct that the commissioner decides` IS `the reduction for my contributory conduct`)

@export By when must I tell the commissioner why a disqualifying circumstance does not apply to me (s 45 (2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice of a disqualifying circumstance` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the commissioner's notice that your application appears to involve a disqualifying circumstance, such as 2027-01-10
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I answer a notice of a disqualifying circumstance` IS
    `the days to answer a notice of a disqualifying circumstance (s 45 (2) (b))` `days after` `the day I received the notice of a disqualifying circumstance`

§§ `Part 4 -- funeral expenses`

-- Situation: someone was killed by murder, manslaughter or culpable driving, and the applicant paid or must pay for the
-- funeral. The s 45 (1) (d) finding is not read for a funeral application (see vocfa-core.l4): a fixed FALSE.

@export Can I get a funeral expense payment for someone killed by homicide, and how much (ss 51 to 54, 60, Regulation s 11)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (if there were 2 or more related acts, the day of the most recent one), as a date such as 2026-03-14
      `the offence` IS AN `Associated offence` @desc The offence in the course of which the act happened. One of: "an offence against the person under the Crimes Act 1900, part 2" (such as assault, wounding, murder or manslaughter); "a sexual offence under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3"; "intimate image abuse under the Crimes Act 1900, part 3A"; "female genital mutilation under the Crimes Act 1900, part 4"; "sexual servitude under the Crimes Act 1900, part 5"; "robbery under the Criminal Code, s 309"; "aggravated robbery under the Criminal Code, s 310"; "an offence listed in schedule 1, division 1.2.2 (family violence offences)" (such as damaging property, arson, burglary, threats to damage property, contravening a family violence order, firearms offences, offensive behaviour, or negligent, furious or menacing driving); "an offence not listed in schedule 1"
      `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person harmed (you, or the person who died) is a current or former domestic or intimate partner of the offender, a relative of the offender, a child of the offender's current or former domestic partner, or a parent of the offender's child
      `whether anyone died` IS A `Death` @desc Whether anyone died. One of: "no one died as a result of the act"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, which was murder, manslaughter or culpable driving causing death"; "a person died as a direct result of the act, in the course of another offence"
      `I have paid or must pay the funeral costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid, or are required to pay, the costs of the funeral of the person who died
      `the reasonable costs of the funeral` IS A NUMBER @desc The reasonable costs of the funeral, in Australian dollars
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died, such as 2026-08-01
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the application, such as 2027-06-30
      `the commissioner finds I conspired with the offender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you conspired with the person responsible for the act of violence (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds my serious crime was the main reason for the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you were involved in a serious crime when the act happened and that crime was the main reason for it (answer no if not)
      `the commissioner finds I unreasonably failed to help the police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has found that you unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police about the act (answer no if not)
      `payments I have received for the funeral costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Other payments you have received because of the death that cover the funeral costs, such as insurance, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Funeral answer`
DECIDE `Can I get a funeral expense payment, and how much` IS
    `the funeral expense answer for` (`Funeral facts` WITH
            `the day of the fatal act` IS `the day of the act of violence`
            `the fatal offence` IS `the offence`
            `the person who died was a relevant person in relation to the offender` IS `the person harmed is a partner or relative of the offender`
            `the way the person died` IS `whether anyone died`
            `the applicant has paid or is required to pay the funeral costs` IS `I have paid or must pay the funeral costs`
            `the reasonable costs of the funeral` IS `the reasonable costs of the funeral`
            `the day of the death` IS `the day the person died`
            `the day of the funeral application` IS `the day I apply`
            `the conduct findings for the funeral application` IS (`Conduct findings` WITH
                `the applicant conspired with the person responsible for the act` IS `the commissioner finds I conspired with the offender`
                `the applicant was involved in a serious crime that was the main reason the act occurred` IS `the commissioner finds my serious crime was the main reason for the act`
                `the act was related to a serious crime carried out by the primary victim` IS FALSE
                `the applicant unreasonably failed to give assistance to the police` IS `the commissioner finds I unreasonably failed to help the police`)
            `associated payments covering the funeral costs` IS `payments I have received for the funeral costs`)

@export What is the last day to apply for a funeral expense payment (s 54)?
GIVEN `the day the person died` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died, such as 2026-08-01
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to apply for a funeral expense payment` IS
    `the last day to apply for a funeral expense payment (s 54)` `the day the person died`

§§ `Part 5 -- telling the commissioner, and repaying`

-- Situation: after the assistance was paid, the applicant received another payment because of the act (damages,
-- workers compensation, insurance, a reparation order).

@export I have received another payment because of the act of violence: must I tell the commissioner, and by when (s 64)?
GIVEN `the payment was made because of the act of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment (damages, workers compensation, insurance, a reparation order or any other amount not under this Act) was paid to you, or to someone for you, as a result of the act of violence
      `I received the payment after my assistance was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received that payment after financial assistance or a funeral expense payment was made to you
      `the day I received the payment` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the payment, such as 2027-02-10
GIVETH A `Notification answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the commissioner about a payment, and by when` IS
    `the s 64 answer for` `the payment was made because of the act of violence` `I received the payment after my assistance was paid` `the day I received the payment`

@export How much might I have to repay to the Territory after receiving another payment for the same harm (s 62)?
GIVEN `the assistance and funeral payment I received` IS A NUMBER @desc The total financial assistance and funeral expense payment you received under the Act, in Australian dollars
      `the part of the payment covering the same harm or loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the other payment that covers the same harm or loss as the assistance was meant to cover, in Australian dollars (0 if it covers something else)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much might I have to repay` IS
    `the repayment amount (s 62)` `the assistance and funeral payment I received` `the part of the payment covering the same harm or loss`

@export By when must I contact the commissioner after a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the repayment arrangement notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the commissioner's repayment arrangement notice, such as 2027-03-01
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I contact the commissioner about repaying` IS
    `the last day to contact the commissioner after a repayment arrangement notice (s 66 (2))` `the day I received the repayment arrangement notice`

@export Am I liable to repay the Territory, or is my liability stayed (ss 65 and 67)?
GIVEN `I received the payment after my assistance was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received that payment after financial assistance or a funeral expense payment was made to you
      `I have been given a repayment direction notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner has given you a repayment direction notice
      `I paid by the repayment date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid the repayment amount on or before the repayment date in the notice
      `I applied to the ACAT by the repayment date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the ACT Civil and Administrative Tribunal for review of the notice on or before the repayment date
      `the ACAT dismissed my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ACAT has dismissed your application for review (answer no if it has not decided)
GIVETH A `Liability answer`
DECIDE `Am I liable to repay` IS
    `the s 65 answer for` (`Repayment position` WITH
            `received the associated payment after the assistance` IS `I received the payment after my assistance was paid`
            `has been given a repayment direction notice` IS `I have been given a repayment direction notice`
            `paid the repayment amount on or before the repayment date` IS `I paid by the repayment date`
            `applied to the ACAT for review on or before the repayment date` IS `I applied to the ACAT by the repayment date`
            `the ACAT dismissed the application for review` IS `the ACAT dismissed my application`)

§§ `Part 9 -- asking for a decision to be reconsidered`

-- Situation: the commissioner has made a decision on the application.

@export By when, and to whom, must I apply to have the commissioner's decision reconsidered or reviewed (s 92, schedule 2)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision` @desc The commissioner's decision. One of: "not to extend the time for making an application (s 32)"; "the amount of financial assistance (s 46)"; "the amount of a reduction of financial assistance (s 47)"; "the variation of an amount of financial assistance (s 50)"; "the suspension of financial assistance (s 63)"; "that applications involve related acts of violence (s 44)"; "that financial assistance is not to be given (s 45)"; "a requirement to repay financial assistance (s 67)"
      `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice of the decision was given to you, such as 2027-04-01
GIVETH A `Review answer`
DECIDE `By when must I ask for a decision to be reconsidered` IS
    `the review answer for` `the decision` `the day I was given notice of the decision`

§§ `Part 10 -- my lawyer's costs`

@export What is the most my lawyer may charge me for an application, or for an appeal or review (s 96, Regulation s 12)?
GIVEN `what the legal services are for` IS A `Legal services` @desc What your lawyer's work is for. One of: "legal services for an application for financial assistance"; "legal services for an appeal or review process under the Act"
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my lawyer may charge me` IS
    `the most a lawyer may charge for` `what the legal services are for`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not answer`

@export Does this encoding answer my question about recovery from the offender, the levy, secrecy, ACAT review, injuries before 1 July 2016, or the commissioner's guidelines?
GIVEN `the topic` IS AN `Other topic` @desc What you want to know about. One of: "recovering the assistance from the offender (part 6)"; "the levy on convicted offenders (part 7)"; "the commissioner's administration, and the secrecy of my information (part 8)"; "how the ACAT reviews a decision (part 9)"; "an application about a criminal injury before 1 July 2016 (s 98)"; "what the commissioner's guidelines say (s 87)"
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
DECIDE `Does this encoding answer my question about` IS
    `the coverage answer for` `the topic`
